// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1047
// Description: Detects execution of wbemtest.exe, the interactive WMI Test GUI. It is rarely used legitimately
//   on endpoints and can be abused to query WMI, instantiate classes for execution, and create
//   persistence (WMI event subscriptions) interactively.
// False positives:
//   - Administrators or developers troubleshooting WMI
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Wbemtest/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8e7b36a9de00c979a098f16eb29c1c22fb63cb4b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wbemtest_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\wbemtest.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wbemtest.exe"
